commandpp — copyright and attribution notice
=============================================

commandpp is an independent re-implementation of the observable behaviour of
the MS-DOS / Windows 95 COMMAND.COM command interpreter, written from scratch
in modern C++. It contains no Microsoft source code, object code or binaries.

Behaviour was derived from the published COMMAND.COM sources (used as a
reference for semantics) and from the command set documented in the user
manual. Implementation code in this repository is original.

MS-DOS, Windows, COMMAND.COM and Microsoft are trademarks of Microsoft
Corporation. The two-line startup banner printed by the interactive shell is
reproduced only because it is part of the original program's observable
output; it is a short factual copyright notice, not a claim of authorship or
endorsement.

The modern C++ implementation in this directory is provided for study and
compatibility testing. Add your own licence terms here if you redistribute it.
